    "mechanistic_diagnosis": "C0 assumes the linear two-branch Prony law is sufficient even after yielding. It is sufficient only when every calibrated historical stress and current hold has absolute magnitude at or below the declared yield stress. C1 retains the Prony response and adds signed squared hold overstress and a transient driven by accumulated plastic work times the current hold, with matching initial-rate terms. Prior overstress can therefore activate C1 even when the hold is subyield. The calibrated history-and-hold maximum is zero on all C0 successes and 3.26200715 on the C0 failure. Hold-only excess misses unloaded histories, and the history integral measures plastic work but misses hold-only yielding. The two matrix features, three circulation-related features, Robin asymmetry, P\u00e9clet proxy, and nuisance condition number are unavailable; coupon missingness concerns alignment, not yielding.",
